Secrets Management in GitOps

✨ Hello DevOps Learners!
Continuing my GitOps learning journey after completing Ansible, today I’m exploring Secrets Management in GitOps — a critical topic for security in real-world DevOps 🚀
Managing sensitive data like passwords, API keys, and tokens in GitOps requires secure approaches.

🔹 Kubernetes Secrets
 Kubernetes provides a built-in way to store sensitive data using Secrets.
Stores data in base64 encoded format
Used by pods and applications
Not fully secure for Git storage

🔹 Sealed Secrets
 Sealed Secrets solve the problem of storing secrets in Git.
Encrypt secrets before storing in Git
Only the Kubernetes cluster can decrypt them
Safe to commit into repositories
This is widely used in GitOps workflows for secure secret handling.

🔹 HashiCorp Vault Integration
 HashiCorp Vault is a powerful tool for managing secrets securely.
Stores secrets centrally
Provides dynamic secrets
Integrates with Kubernetes and GitOps tools
It ensures enterprise-level security for sensitive data.

🔹 Why Secrets Management is Important
Prevents data leaks
Secures production environments
Enables safe GitOps workflows

💡 Key Insight:
 In GitOps, secrets should never be stored in plain text — always use encryption or dedicated tools like Sealed Secrets or Vault.
